Florian,
On 18.02.25 12:10, Marc Strämke wrote:
>>> We're using Dovetail on x86, but: I think all of our boards are Intel
>>> based while yours is an AMD. There might be a small but significant
>>> difference (code wise) somewhere, but as a kvm / virtual target is also
>>> affected that's kind of unlikely.
>>>
>>> Let me try to build one of your configurations that does not boot up on
>>> top of KVM. Might take a couple of days...
>> I finally got xenomai-images to build and the result boots on my 
>> machine. I will try to figure out what the differences between both 
>> are kernel wise.
>
> I have to correct this: KVM runs with -cpu host , which was given by 
> the script in xenomai-images but not by me. If i run qemu with kvm and 
> -cpu host flag my kernel boots just fine. 

When i boot the machine with  xenomai.state=stopped  on the kernel 
command line it boots successfully.  Also later activation of xenomai 
seems to not cause any issues.

Does this give you any insight?

Bootlog attached from the AMD target machine. It does indeed switch to 
TSC as a clocksource.

Just a thought: can it be that it runs when the xenomai domain gets 
activated when the TSC is the clocksource, but not when during the TSC 
calibration refinement the clocksoruce seems to be the acpi_pm?

I have further found out that if i give clocksource=hpet as kernel 
parameter the kernel boots(second bootlog). From my look at the log this 
only changes timing: Somehow Xenomai as IRQ pipeline head then gets 
initialized later. Clocksource is HPET for a short amount of time during 
the boot but does the same switching to TSC with calibration by the 
ACPI_PM.




Marc

